      "body": "*@yringler commented on May 27, 2019, 8:03 PM UTC:*\r\n\r\nThis is similar to [#1518](https://github.com/Dart-Code/Dart-Code/issues/1518)\r\nI set up flutter/dart, I can run everything fine from VS Code, the debugger hits the breakpoint - then it loses device connection, and `adb devices` shows my device as offline.\r\n(Running [this code lab](https://codelabs.developers.google.com/codelabs/first-flutter-app-pt1/)\r\n\r\nOutput of `flutter doctor`\r\n\r\n> [\u221a] Flutter (Channel stable, v1.5.4-hotfix.2, on Microsoft Windows [Version 10.0.17763.503], locale en-US)\r\n> \r\n> [\u221a] Android toolchain - develop for Android devices (Android SDK version 28.0.3)\r\n> [\u221a] Android Studio (version 3.3)\r\n> [\u221a] VS Code (version 1.34.0)\r\n> [\u221a] VS Code, 64-bit edition (version 1.28.1)\r\n> [!] Connected device\r\n\r\nOutput of log, with **Flutter Run** and **Debugger (Observatory)**: https://gist.github.com/DanTup/c05f196729d047edef9e0db338e648f0\r\n\r\n*This issue was moved by [DanTup](https://github.com/DanTup) from [Dart-Code/Dart-Code#1754](https://github.com/Dart-Code/Dart-Code/issues/1754).*",
